       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day, and that is the ceiling for inpatient prescribing. At 6,400 mg/day the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up substantially.\n\nHere are some possible intended orders:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily**, which is 3,200 mg/day. This is the maximum for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013800 mg PO three times daily**, which is 1,200\u20132,400 mg/day. This is typical for pain or inflammation.\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily. Maybe that was the intended total.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm that you really want 1600 mg four times daily. If you do, I'll need the clinical rationale for the order note. I can also add a note such as \"take with food\" or \"limit duration.\""
